// array_add to a resizable array whose count was set below 0 (issue #158,
// spec 3.17, 8.1): the add would write its item before data's memory, and
// no index of its own is checked, so the array's count is, and the program
// stops at the built-in's name.
main :: () {
    a : [..]int;
    a.count = -3;
    array_add(*a, 1);
}
